## Explain lazy history and collaborative exchange

Scalar depicts commit/tree/blob history, pruning, publishing, full-history setup, shallow setup, and on-demand retrieval. A later request added a fourth commit and a third user. Exchange moved from object graphs to a clearer keeper story: both keepers edit a shared ancestor, the first publisher advances the record, the second is rejected, merges locally, then republishes. Local string choice, set union, and list appends are scoped examples; the record is append-only and rejected updates never enter it. The performance view uses dinosaur neck lengths with numeric reference lines.

